  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-05d47561fd0f-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, the case asks whether non\u2011lawyer parents of a child with a disability may bring an IDEA claim in federal court without an attorney."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-05d47561fd0f-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue that parents are \u201creal parties in interest\u201d in IDEA suits regardless of the specific claims asserted."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-05d47561fd0f-0000-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, petitioners assert that parents are real parties in interest in IDEA suits."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Salmons",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-05d47561fd0f-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 21,
                "start": 21
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Salmons, the term \u201cfree appropriate public education\u201d means special\u2011education services provided without charge and at no cost to parents."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Bergeron",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-05d47561fd0f-0001-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 28,
                "start": 28
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Bergeron, the common\u2011law rule banning parental pro\u202fse representation is longstanding and pervasive."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Bergeron",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-05d47561fd0f-0001-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 28,
                "start": 28
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Bergeron, petitioners characterize the right to representation as a remedy, not a substantive right."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Bergeron",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-05d47561fd0f-0001-0007"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 30,
                "start": 30
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Bergeron, any reimbursement claim would be paid to the child, who is the proper party to bring the claim."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-05d47561fd0f-0003-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 58,
                "start": 58
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, petitioners suggest that the attorney\u2011fee provision and the timing of the Maroni decision in the First Circuit may be relevant."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-05d47561fd0f-0003-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 59,
                "start": 59
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Petitioners argue that the Court\u2019s spending\u2011clause jurisprudence is concerned with giving states clear notice of liability and fiscal obligations."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioners' Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
